70,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Okay, let's see! Textiles (A) seems local, so transport is cheap. Maritime (C) has loans, which sounds expensive. City (D) has a working bench!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, City (D) is a problem. A working conservation bench in the gallery? Our lab is already drowning in a backlog!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,1,talk,Shion,,"But look at the visitor data! City (D) and Textiles (A) both have that ""working"" element people love. Light and Motion (B) has mechanisms!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Light and Motion (B) is a nightmare. Overhead rigging in the suspended bay? And darkened zones will interfere with evening hire bookings.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, Light and Motion (B) also sounds like a maintenance disaster. Remember the powered display logs? I can't support that.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,2,talk,Mio,,"If we do Textiles (A), it's local, so we save on transport and maybe the joiner's rates are lower. It sounds very safe!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,2,talk,Victoria,,Textiles (A) is manageable. The volunteers are town historians; they would be perfect for talking about local weaving and dyeing.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Maritime (C) is too static. It's just cased objects. Textiles (A) has demonstration sessions, which is exactly what the comment slips asked for.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Textiles (A) is lightweight and flexible. It won't break the suspended bay or block the caterers during evening events.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"And since it's local, we avoid the nightmare of distant lender paperwork and shipping cut-offs. It's the most reliable choice.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm totally for Textiles (A)! It saves money and sounds super friendly!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. It aligns with our volunteer strengths and doesn't add to the conservation backlog.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It satisfies the desire for a ""living"" exhibition. I am convinced.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It is the only candidate that doesn't clash with the building's structural or operational limits.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is the most peaceful path. No shipping delays, no broken motors. I am in agreement.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
85,3,4,talk,Mio,,Yay! We all agree! I vote for Textiles of the Region!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
86,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
